 "_doc": "Rand West City LM. Two layouts, both handled: (a) 'TAX INVOICE / STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT' with labelled 'Account Number:/Account Date:/Street:/Deposit:' and lines 'units@ tariff * value'; (b) 'Tax Invoice / Satement' with label-above-value header and lines 'units tariff value' (may run to two pages). Both print a Meter Readings table whose rows carry a LEVIED AMOUNT. Electricity (ex VAT, one VAT line per bill): 'TOU LV ABOVE nnKVA' (basic) + 'LV SUPPLY ACCESS CHARGE KVA' (both other_r; access units equal the measured kVA so nmd is left blank), 'LV SUPPLY DEMAND CHARGE KVA' (demand), 'LV SUPPLY LOW|HIGH SEASON OFF PEAK|PEAK|STANDARD' (TOU kWh + Rand, summed across seasons when a bill straddles the season change). meter/read period from the first TIME OF USE row; start/end readings blank (three registers). Fingerprint: municipal VAT number + name. IDENTITY: rw_elec_by_meter_r = sum of Meter Readings levied amounts (KVA/ELECTRICITY/TIME OF USE rows) + basic vs total_ex_vat_r: R0.00 on 9/9. The 10th file is a rotated scan whose OCR is word-salad: deliberately unrouted. Checked on 9 readable bills.",
